---
import PlaygroundShell from '../components/PlaygroundShell.astro';
import RangeField from '../components/RangeField.astro';
const slots = Array.from({ length: 16 }, (_, i) => i);
---
<PlaygroundShell title="Simulate it" hint="600 account events (deposit, withdraw) for 40 accounts arrive 1 ms apart and each takes 6 to 14 ms. Account acct-0 is hot. Pick how the topic is split and watch order and throughput.">
  <ol class="how">
    <li>The default is <b>one queue with 4 competing consumers</b> and 30% of the traffic on one account: it processes about 404 events/s, but 21 events finish after a later event of the same account, and 3 withdrawals run before the deposit that funds them (<b>overdraft errors</b>), leaving 2 accounts with the wrong balance. Set <b>consumers</b> to 1 and order is perfect, at about 101 events/s.</li>
    <li>Switch to <b>Partitioned by account</b> with 8 partitions and <b>consumers</b> set to 8: <b>0 violations</b> at any consumer count, but throughput drops to about 238 events/s because the hot account's partition holds 252 of the 600 events and its single consumer is 99% busy while the others sit at 12 to 28%. More consumers do not help (16 consumers: still 238); set <b>hot account share</b> to 0 and it rises to about 557.</li>
    <li>Turn on failures. With <b>Retry later</b> (the failed event goes back behind its successors) key partitioning loses its guarantee: 40 violations and 7 overdrafts at 8 partitions and 8 consumers. <b>Retry in place</b> keeps 0 violations but blocks the partition: throughput falls to about 206. Tick <b>Reorder buffer</b> to hold early events until their predecessors arrive: overdrafts go to 0, but 191 events are held, the worst for about 1.9 s.</li>
    <li>Partitioned, 8 partitions, 8 consumers: set <b>change partitions to</b> 4 at the 50% mark. The 23 accounts whose placement changed now go to partitions that are already draining, and 84 events finish after a later event of their account. Changing to 12 gives 17 violations: the reshuffle costs order while the old backlog drains, even though the key is the same.</li>
  </ol>
  <div class="pg op" data-op>
    <div class="pg-row">
      <label>Transport <select class="pg-in" data-transport>
        <option value="queue" selected>One queue, competing consumers</option>
        <option value="partitioned">Partitioned by account id</option>
        <option value="single">Single partition (global order)</option>
      </select></label>
      <RangeField label="Consumers" name="consumers" min="1" max="16" value="4" readout="4" />
      <label>Partitions <select class="pg-in" data-partitions>
        <option>2</option><option>4</option><option selected>8</option><option>12</option><option>16</option>
      </select></label>
      <label>Hot account share <input type="range" min="0" max="60" step="5" value="30" data-hot /> <b data-hotval>30</b>%</label>
    </div>
    <div class="pg-row">
      <label>On failure (8% of attempts) <select class="pg-in" data-retry>
        <option value="none" selected>No failures</option>
        <option value="inplace">Retry in place (block the partition)</option>
        <option value="later">Retry later (back of the line)</option>
      </select></label>
      <label>Change partitions to <select class="pg-in" data-repart>
        <option value="0" selected>No change</option><option>3</option><option>4</option><option>6</option><option>12</option><option>16</option>
      </select></label>
      <label>at <input type="range" min="20" max="80" step="10" value="50" data-repat /> <b data-repatval>50</b>% of the stream</label>
      <label class="op-check"><input type="checkbox" data-buffer /> Reorder buffer (sequence numbers)</label>
    </div>
    <div class="pg-row"><button class="btn" type="button" data-reset>Reset to defaults</button></div>
    <p class="pg-out" data-verdict aria-live="polite"></p>
    <div class="pg-grid">
      <div class="pg-box" style="--c: var(--role-1)"><h3>Throughput</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-thr></span><span class="pg-note" data-thrnote></span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" data-violbox><h3>Order violations</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-viol></span><span class="pg-note" data-violnote></span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" data-odbox><h3>Overdraft errors</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-od></span><span class="pg-note" data-odnote></span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" style="--c: var(--role-3)"><h3>p95 latency</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-lat></span><span class="pg-note" data-latnote></span></div>
    </div>
    <h3>Events per partition (hot ones in red)</h3>
    <div class="op-bars" data-loadbars>
      {slots.map((i) => <div class="op-bar" data-lrow><span class="pg-mono">{i === 0 ? 'P0' : 'P' + i}</span><span class="op-track"><span class="op-fill" data-lfill></span></span><span class="pg-mono" data-lval></span></div>)}
    </div>
    <h3>Consumer busy time</h3>
    <div class="op-bars" data-utilbars>
      {slots.map((i) => <div class="op-bar" data-urow><span class="pg-mono">C{i}</span><span class="op-track"><span class="op-fill" data-ufill></span></span><span class="pg-mono" data-uval></span></div>)}
    </div>
    <h3>Same stream and settings, all three transports</h3>
    <div class="op-scroll" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Comparison of the three transports">
      <table class="op-table">
        <thead><tr><th scope="col">Transport</th><th scope="col">events/s</th><th scope="col">violations</th><th scope="col">overdrafts</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody data-cmp></tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="pg-note">Assumptions: 600 events, 40 accounts, arrivals 1 ms apart (faster than the consumers, so queues build up), processing 6 to 14 ms, a failed attempt costs a full processing time, retry in place waits 5 ms, retry later re-queues after 30 ms, partition owner = partition mod consumers (a static assignment, no rebalance pause). A violation is an event that finishes after a later event of the same account. Seeded, so the numbers repeat.</p>
  </div>
</PlaygroundShell>
<script>
  import { query, mulberry32 } from '../playground';
  const KEYS = 40, N = 600, FAIL_PCT = 8, BACKOFF = 5, LATER = 30, SEED = 42;
  const MAX_FAILS = 3; // failed attempts drawn per event, at most
  const LOW_BALANCE = 20; // below this an account only receives deposits
  const DEPOSIT = { min: 20, span: 41 }; const WITHDRAW_MIN = 10; // amounts; a withdrawal never exceeds the balance
  const PROC = { minMs: 6, spanMs: 9 }; // processing time per event
  const MS_PER_S = 1000; const P95 = 0.95;
  const HOT_LOAD_FACTOR = 1.5; // a partition with this many times the mean load is marked hot
  const NEVER_HOT = 1e9; const UTIL_NEVER_HOT = 101; // thresholds no bar can reach
  interface Ev { id: number; key: number; seq: number; deposit: boolean; amount: number; proc: number; nfail: number; arrival: number }
  interface Stream { ev: Ev[]; finalBal: number[] }
  interface Cfg { transport: 'queue' | 'partitioned' | 'single'; consumers: number; partitions: number; retry: 'none' | 'inplace' | 'later'; repartTo: number; repartAt: number; buffer: boolean }
  interface Item { id: number; avail: number }

  // FNV-1a string hash and mulberry32 PRNG
  function fnv1a(s: string): number { let h = 0x811c9dc5; for (let i = 0; i < s.length; i++) { h ^= s.charCodeAt(i); h = Math.imul(h, 0x01000193) >>> 0; } return h >>> 0; }
  const keyHash: number[] = []; for (let k = 0; k < KEYS; k++) keyHash.push(fnv1a('acct-' + k));

  function genStream(hotPct: number): Stream {
    const rnd = mulberry32(SEED); const bal: number[] = new Array(KEYS).fill(0); const nseq: number[] = new Array(KEYS).fill(0); const ev: Ev[] = [];
    for (let id = 0; id < N; id++) {
      const u = rnd(), v = rnd(), w = rnd(), a = rnd(), p = rnd();
      const key = u * 100 < hotPct ? 0 : 1 + Math.floor(v * (KEYS - 1));
      let nf = 0; let ok = true; for (let j = 0; j < MAX_FAILS; j++) { const d = rnd(); if (ok && d * 100 < FAIL_PCT) nf++; else ok = false; }
      const deposit = bal[key] < LOW_BALANCE || w < 0.5;
      const amount = deposit ? DEPOSIT.min + Math.floor(a * DEPOSIT.span) : WITHDRAW_MIN + Math.floor(a * (bal[key] - (WITHDRAW_MIN - 1)));
      bal[key] += deposit ? amount : -amount;
      ev.push({ id, key, seq: nseq[key]++, deposit, amount, proc: PROC.minMs + Math.floor(p * PROC.spanMs), nfail: nf, arrival: id });
    }
    return { ev, finalBal: bal };
  }
  function insert(q: Item[], item: Item) { let i = q.length; while (i > 0 && q[i - 1].avail > item.avail) i--; q.splice(i, 0, item); }

  function simulate(stream: Stream, cfg: Cfg) {
    const { ev } = stream;
    const part = cfg.transport === 'partitioned' ? cfg.partitions : 1;
    const to = cfg.transport === 'partitioned' && cfg.repartTo > 0 ? cfg.repartTo : part;
    const nq = Math.max(part, to); const cut = Math.floor(N * cfg.repartAt / 100);
    const C = cfg.transport === 'single' ? 1 : cfg.consumers;
    const route = (e: Ev) => cfg.transport === 'partitioned' ? keyHash[e.key] % (e.id < cut ? part : to) : 0;
    const qs: Item[][] = []; for (let i = 0; i < nq; i++) qs.push([]);
    const load: number[] = new Array(nq).fill(0);
    for (const e of ev) { const qi = route(e); load[qi]++; qs[qi].push({ id: e.id, avail: e.arrival }); }
    const mine: number[][] = []; for (let c = 0; c < C; c++) mine.push([]);
    for (let qi = 0; qi < nq; qi++) { if (cfg.transport === 'queue') for (let c = 0; c < C; c++) mine[c].push(qi); else mine[qi % C].push(qi); }
    const free: number[] = new Array(C).fill(0); const busy: number[] = new Array(C).fill(0);
    const done: number[] = new Array(N).fill(-1); const attempts: number[] = new Array(N).fill(0);
    for (;;) {
      let bc = -1, bq = -1, bs = 0, ba = 0;
      for (let c = 0; c < C; c++) for (const qi of mine[c]) {
        const h = qs[qi][0]; if (!h) continue; const s = Math.max(free[c], h.avail);
        if (bc < 0 || s < bs || (s === bs && h.avail < ba)) { bc = c; bq = qi; bs = s; ba = h.avail; }
      }
      if (bc < 0) break;
      const q = qs[bq]; const e = ev[q[0].id]; const nf = cfg.retry === 'none' ? 0 : e.nfail;
      if (cfg.retry === 'later' && attempts[e.id] < nf) {
        const end = bs + e.proc; busy[bc] += e.proc; free[bc] = end; attempts[e.id]++;
        const it = q.shift()!; it.avail = end + LATER; insert(q, it);
      } else {
        const tries = cfg.retry === 'later' ? 1 : nf + 1; const end = bs + tries * e.proc + (tries - 1) * BACKOFF;
        busy[bc] += tries * e.proc; free[bc] = end; done[e.id] = end; q.shift();
      }
    }
    const order = ev.map((e) => e.id).sort((a, b) => done[a] - done[b] || a - b);
    const maxSeq: number[] = new Array(KEYS).fill(-1); const bad = new Set<number>(); let violations = 0;
    for (const id of order) { const e = ev[id]; if (e.seq < maxSeq[e.key]) { violations++; bad.add(e.key); } else maxSeq[e.key] = e.seq; }
    const apply = done.slice(); let applyOrder = order;
    if (cfg.buffer) {
      const run: number[] = new Array(KEYS).fill(0);
      for (const e of ev) { run[e.key] = Math.max(run[e.key], done[e.id]); apply[e.id] = run[e.key]; }
      applyOrder = ev.map((e) => e.id).sort((a, b) => apply[a] - apply[b] || ev[a].seq - ev[b].seq || a - b);
    }
    const bal: number[] = new Array(KEYS).fill(0); let overdrafts = 0;
    for (const id of applyOrder) { const e = ev[id]; if (e.deposit) bal[e.key] += e.amount; else if (bal[e.key] >= e.amount) bal[e.key] -= e.amount; else overdrafts++; }
    let wrong = 0; for (let k = 0; k < KEYS; k++) if (bal[k] !== stream.finalBal[k]) wrong++;
    const makespan = Math.max(...done); const lat = ev.map((e) => apply[e.id] - e.arrival).sort((a, b) => a - b);
    let held = 0, worst = 0; for (const e of ev) { const w = apply[e.id] - done[e.id]; if (w > 0) held++; if (w > worst) worst = w; }
    let moved = 0; if (to !== part) { const seen = new Set(ev.map((e) => e.key)); seen.forEach((k) => { if (keyHash[k] % part !== keyHash[k] % to) moved++; }); }
    return { throughput: Math.floor(N * MS_PER_S / makespan), makespan, violations, badKeys: bad.size, overdrafts, wrong, load, util: busy.map((b) => Math.floor(100 * b / makespan)), p95: lat[Math.floor(P95 * (N - 1))], held, worst, moved, nq, consumers: C };
  }
  type Res = ReturnType<typeof simulate>;

  document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-op]').forEach((root) => {
    const q = query(root);
    const inp = (s: string) => q<HTMLInputElement>(s);
    const sel = (s: string) => q<HTMLSelectElement>(s);
    const lrows = Array.from(root.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-lrow]')); const urows = Array.from(root.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-urow]'));
    const streams = new Map<number, Stream>();
    const stream = (h: number) => { let s = streams.get(h); if (!s) { s = genStream(h); streams.set(h, s); } return s; };
    const NAMES = { queue: 'One queue, competing', partitioned: 'Partitioned by account', single: 'Single partition' };
    let raf = 0;

    function readCfg(): Cfg {
      return { transport: sel('[data-transport]').value as Cfg['transport'], consumers: Number(inp('[data-consumers]').value), partitions: Number(sel('[data-partitions]').value),
        retry: sel('[data-retry]').value as Cfg['retry'], repartTo: Number(sel('[data-repart]').value), repartAt: Number(inp('[data-repat]').value), buffer: inp('[data-buffer]').checked };
    }
    function bars(rows: HTMLElement[], vals: number[], max: number, hotFrom: number, fillSel: string, valSel: string, unit: string) {
      rows.forEach((row, i) => {
        row.hidden = i >= vals.length; if (i >= vals.length) return;
        const f = row.querySelector<HTMLElement>(fillSel)!; f.style.width = Math.max(1, Math.round(100 * vals[i] / max)) + '%';
        f.style.background = vals[i] >= hotFrom ? 'var(--bad)' : 'var(--role-2)';
        row.querySelector<HTMLElement>(valSel)!.textContent = vals[i] + unit;
      });
    }
    function verdict(cfg: Cfg, r: Res): string {
      const out: string[] = [];
      if (cfg.transport === 'single') out.push('A single partition has one reader, so everything is totally ordered and nothing scales: extra consumers sit idle.');
      else if (cfg.transport === 'queue' && cfg.consumers === 1 && r.violations === 0) out.push('One consumer drains the queue in order, so nothing is reordered, but throughput is whatever one consumer can do.');
      else if (r.violations === 0) out.push('Per-account order held: no event finished after a later event of its account.');
      else if (cfg.buffer) out.push(`${r.violations} events finished after a later event of the same account (${r.badKeys} of ${KEYS} accounts), but the reorder buffer held ${r.held} events (worst wait ${r.worst} ms) until their predecessors were applied: ${r.overdrafts} overdrafts, ${r.wrong} wrong balances.`);
      else out.push(`${r.violations} events finished after a later event of the same account (${r.badKeys} of ${KEYS} accounts). Applied in that order the ledger rejects ${r.overdrafts} withdrawals as overdrafts and ${r.wrong} accounts end with the wrong balance.`);
      if (cfg.transport === 'partitioned') {
        const top = Math.max(...r.load); const even = Math.round(100 / r.nq);
        out.push(`The busiest partition has ${Math.round(100 * top / N)}% of the events (an even split would be ${even}%); it finishes last and sets the throughput.`);
        if (r.moved > 0) out.push(`${r.moved} accounts changed partition mid-stream.`);
      }
      return out.join(' ');
    }
    function draw() {
      raf = 0; const cfg = readCfg(); const hot = Number(inp('[data-hot]').value); const st = stream(hot); const r = simulate(st, cfg);
      q('[data-consumersval]').textContent = String(cfg.consumers); q('[data-hotval]').textContent = String(hot); q('[data-repatval]').textContent = String(cfg.repartAt);
      const part = cfg.transport === 'partitioned';
      sel('[data-partitions]').disabled = !part; sel('[data-repart]').disabled = !part; inp('[data-repat]').disabled = !part || cfg.repartTo === 0;
      inp('[data-consumers]').disabled = cfg.transport === 'single';
      q('[data-verdict]').textContent = verdict(cfg, r);
      q('[data-thr]').textContent = `${r.throughput} events/s`;
      q('[data-thrnote]').textContent = `${N} events in ${(r.makespan / 1000).toFixed(2)} s with ${r.consumers} working consumer${r.consumers === 1 ? '' : 's'}`;
      q('[data-viol]').textContent = String(r.violations);
      q('[data-violnote]').textContent = r.violations === 0 ? 'every account applied in send order' : `${r.badKeys} of ${KEYS} accounts affected`;
      q('[data-odbox]').style.setProperty('--c', r.overdrafts > 0 ? 'var(--bad)' : 'var(--good)');
      q('[data-violbox]').style.setProperty('--c', r.violations > 0 ? 'var(--bad)' : 'var(--good)');
      q('[data-od]').textContent = String(r.overdrafts);
      q('[data-odnote]').textContent = `withdrawals rejected; ${r.wrong} accounts with a wrong final balance`;
      q('[data-lat]').textContent = `${r.p95} ms`;
      q('[data-latnote]').textContent = cfg.buffer ? `includes buffering (${r.held} events held)` : 'arrival until the consumer finished it';
      const mean = N / r.nq; const mx = Math.max(...r.load);
      bars(lrows, r.load, mx, part || r.nq > 1 ? HOT_LOAD_FACTOR * mean : NEVER_HOT, '[data-lfill]', '[data-lval]', '');
      bars(urows, r.util, 100, UTIL_NEVER_HOT, '[data-ufill]', '[data-uval]', '%');
      const body = q('[data-cmp]'); const rows: string[] = [];
      (['queue', 'partitioned', 'single'] as const).forEach((t) => {
        const x = simulate(st, { ...cfg, transport: t });
        rows.push(`<tr class="${t === cfg.transport ? 'cur' : ''}"><th scope="row">${NAMES[t]}</th><td>${x.throughput}</td><td>${x.violations}</td><td>${x.overdrafts}</td></tr>`);
      });
      body.innerHTML = rows.join('');
    }
    function schedule() { if (!raf) raf = requestAnimationFrame(draw); }
    function reset() {
      sel('[data-transport]').value = 'queue'; inp('[data-consumers]').value = '4'; sel('[data-partitions]').value = '8'; inp('[data-hot]').value = '30';
      sel('[data-retry]').value = 'none'; sel('[data-repart]').value = '0'; inp('[data-repat]').value = '50'; inp('[data-buffer]').checked = false; draw();
    }
    root.querySelectorAll('input, select').forEach((el) => el.addEventListener(el instanceof HTMLInputElement && el.type === 'range' ? 'input' : 'change', schedule));
    q('[data-reset]').addEventListener('click', reset);
    draw();
  });
</script>
<style is:global>
  .playground .op-check { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 6px; }
  .playground .op h3 { margin: 14px 0 6px; font-size: .95rem; }
  .playground .op-bars { display: grid; gap: 3px; }
  .playground .op-bar { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 2.2rem minmax(0, 1fr) 3.2rem; gap: 8px; align-items: center; }
  .playground .op-bar[hidden] { display: none; }
  .playground .op-track { display: block; height: 10px; border-radius: 5px; background: var(--surface-2); overflow: hidden; }
  .playground .op-fill { display: block; height: 100%; border-radius: 5px; transition: width .25s; }
  .playground .op-scroll { overflow-x: auto; }
  .playground .op-table { border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; font-size: .9rem; }
  .playground .op-table th, .playground .op-table td { padding: 6px 10px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); text-align: right; white-space: nowrap; }
  .playground .op-table th:first-child { text-align: left; }
  .playground .op-table tr.cur { background: var(--accent-soft); font-weight: 600; }
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) { .playground .op-fill { transition: none; } }
</style>
